IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-dates`
IMPORT `voc-rules`
IMPORT `voc-seat`

-- Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022 (Vic) -- worked cases for the victim's questions (voc-seat.l4),
-- the deadline rules and the date helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied
-- from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative. Breached traces are asserted with CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS cannot test a breach).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

`an assault` MEANS `an offence punishable by imprisonment involving assault, injury or a threat of injury to a person`
`against me` MEANS `the act of violence was committed against me`
`exposed` MEANS `hearing, witnessing or otherwise being exposed to the effects of the act of violence`
`witnessed` MEANS `I was present at the scene and witnessed it`
`afterwards` MEANS `I became aware of it afterwards`
`psych` MEANS `psychological or psychiatric harm`
`physical` MEANS `actual physical harm`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2028
#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2000
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year` 1900)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year` 2027)
-- 29 February plus 3 years falls on 28 February 2027; 31 August plus 6 months on 28 February 2026, and on 29 February
-- in 2028; 15 December plus 1 month crosses the year.
#ASSERT `the same day` 3 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the same day` 1 `months after` (`d` 15 12 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `d` 29 7 2026
#ASSERT `a person born on` (`d` 11 3 2007) `was under` 18 `on` (`d` 10 3 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person born on` (`d` 10 3 2007) `was under` 18 `on` (`d` 10 3 2025))

§§ `s 9 -- primary victims`

-- Arguments: offence, in Victoria, injury or death resulted, how, harm, direct result, under 18, prescribed category,
-- committed it.
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `a sexual offence` TRUE TRUE `against me` `psych` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` FALSE TRUE `against me` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` TRUE TRUE `against me` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `harm arising only from loss of or damage to property` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `grief or distress only` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `trauma the scheme decision maker has determined to be an injury` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `trauma not determined to be an injury` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `an exacerbation of a pre-existing physical, psychological or psychiatric injury` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `physical` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `against me` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9(2): "whether or not an act of violence is actually committed".
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` FALSE FALSE `trying to prevent an act of violence` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` FALSE FALSE `trying to arrest someone I believed on reasonable grounds had committed an act of violence` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` FALSE FALSE `trying to aid or rescue someone I believed on reasonable grounds was a victim of an act of violence` `psych` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 9(3): a child exposed to it; an adult exposed is not a primary victim (but may be a secondary victim).
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `exposed` `psych` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `an assault` TRUE TRUE `exposed` `psych` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9(4): a prescribed category; s 9(6) still excludes the offender.
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `no harm` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `no harm` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a primary victim` `none of these` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `physical` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

