§§ `ss 16, 18 -- a related victim's amount`

-- Arguments: counselling, medical, distress, lost support, death expenses, other recovery, exceptional, maximum in force,
-- damages received, insurance received, likely payments counted, likely insurance counted, interim paid.
-- 2000 + 1000 + 10000 + 30000 + 5000 = 48000; with the 3000 other in exceptional circumstances 51000, capped at 50000.
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 48000
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 TRUE 51000 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 51000
-- s 18(2): insurance of 45000 cannot touch the 10000 for distress: 48000 - 38000 = 10000; 50000 - 40000 = 10000.
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 FALSE 0 0 45000 0 0 0 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 TRUE 0 0 45000 0 0 0 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 45000 0 EQUALS 10000
-- Other damages reduce the distress amount too: 48000 - 45000 = 3000.
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 FALSE 0 45000 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 2000 1000 10000 30000 5000 3000 FALSE 0 0 5000 0 0 1000 EQUALS 42000
-- Distress above the cap: 50000 is all distress, so insurance takes nothing.
#ASSERT `How much can I be paid as a related victim` 0 0 60000 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 10000 0 0 0 EQUALS 50000

