§§ `ss 44, 45, 46 -- review`

-- Arguments: kind, who decided, day of the notice, extended, extended to (then the day I apply). 1 July + 28 days = 29 July.
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `a refusal of my application, or a requirement to repay interim assistance` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `internal review by the scheme decision maker, applying in writing (s 45)` (`d` 29 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `the amount of assistance` `the scheme decision maker personally` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `review by VCAT (s 46)` (`d` 29 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `a decision about interim assistance` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `none: decisions about interim assistance are not reviewable (s 44(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `another decision` `the scheme decision maker personally` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `none: it is not a reviewable decision (s 44(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `the amount of assistance` `the scheme decision maker on an internal review` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `review by VCAT (s 46)` (`d` 29 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `a requirement to repay assistance, or the amount to repay` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 9 2026) EQUALS `internal review by the scheme decision maker, applying in writing (s 45)` (`d` 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `a refusal to vary my assistance` `the scheme decision maker personally` (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 9 2026) EQUALS `review by VCAT (s 46)` (`d` 29 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I have the decision reviewed` `the amount on my application to vary` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `internal review by the scheme decision maker, applying in writing (s 45)` (`d` 29 7 2026)

#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `a refusal of my application, or a requirement to repay interim assistance` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 29 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `a refusal of my application, or a requirement to repay interim assistance` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 30 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `a requirement to repay assistance, or the amount to repay` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 9 2026) (`d` 15 9 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `a requirement to repay assistance, or the amount to repay` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 9 2026) (`d` 16 9 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `the amount of assistance` `the scheme decision maker personally` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 29 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `the amount of assistance` `the scheme decision maker personally` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 30 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` `a decision about interim assistance` `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 2 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 48, 50 -- variation and repayment`

#ASSERT `By when can I apply to vary my assistance` (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 1 1 1990) FALSE EQUALS `until the last day` (`d` 1 7 2036) "s 48(2)(a)"
#ASSERT `By when can I apply to vary my assistance` (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE EQUALS `until the last day` (`d` 31 12 2042) "s 48(2)(b)"
#ASSERT `By when can I apply to vary my assistance` (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS `the longer time the regulations prescribe (s 48(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `By when can I apply to vary my assistance` (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 1 7 2008) FALSE EQUALS `until the last day` (`d` 1 7 2036) "s 48(2)(a)"
#ASSERT `By when can I apply to vary my assistance` (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 2 7 2008) FALSE EQUALS `until the last day` (`d` 1 7 2036) "s 48(2)(b)"

#ASSERT `The most I can be required to repay` 20000 5000 0 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `The most I can be required to repay` 20000 30000 0 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `The most I can be required to repay` 20000 20000 0 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `The most I can be required to repay` 20000 5000 3000 EQUALS 8000
#ASSERT `The most I can be required to repay` 20000 15000 10000 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `The most I can be required to repay` 20000 0 4000 EQUALS 4000

§§ `s 74 -- varying an old Tribunal award`

-- Arguments: day of the award, date of birth, day I apply, kind, already applied for a substantive variation.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to vary my Tribunal award` (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 3 2026) `a substantive variation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to vary my Tribunal award` (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 2 3 2026) `a substantive variation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to vary my Tribunal award` (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 6 2005) (`d` 31 5 2029) `a substantive variation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to vary my Tribunal award` (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 6 2005) (`d` 1 6 2029) `a substantive variation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to vary my Tribunal award` (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 3 2025) `a substantive variation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to vary my Tribunal award` (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 3 2025) `a minor variation, to give effect to the original intention of the award` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
